NV_PK(39,{"the national chiang kai shek memorial hall opened in 1980 and its roof has eight sides and blue tiles":"","on yangmingshan hydrangea fields like this bloom from may to june":"","a hydrangea ball looks like many flowers but most of the colorful parts are sepals":"","soil can change a hydrangea's color acidic soil makes it bluer and alkaline soil makes it pinker":"","big round hydrangeas like these are called mopheads because they look like the head of a mop":"","the lin family built this house from 1783 to 1785 and it is one of taipei's oldest houses":"","this southern fujian style house was taken apart and rebuilt here to make room for a wider dunhua south road":"","the red sedan chair has the sign for double happiness and in the past a bride rode in one like it on her wedding day":"","a small red brick building sits by a pond full of water lilies next to a weeping willow":"","banana plants ferns and rocks line this garden path":"","this white wall has a door shaped like a vase and a window shaped like a butterfly":"","this gate has five arches and its liberty square sign was put up in 2007":""});